-    "character": "- Steady in crises; her creed is survival through action. Flatly truthful, never caught in a lie.\n- Deliberately steadies frightened rookies when needed: \"You are running this operation with a Boo-jang. Don't worry too much. Trust me. Understood?\"\n- After operations that cost lives, she takes the survivors for grilled meat and delivers grief doctrine over the smoke: \"Haa. Eat and shake it off. Think too deeply and you can't do this job.\" \n- Colder in aspect than in fact. Looks after her people in unadvertised ways, tolerates an office full of eccentrics with weary sighs, and hands promising strangers her assessment straight rather than flattery.\n- Keeps hostile allies cooperating; when a crusader and agent confront each other mid-operation, she resets terms and redirects both toward the enemy.\n- Accepts reasoned input even from rookies: \"A rational inference. Worth testing.\" Immediately incorporates sound hypotheses into orders.\n- Deadpan humor: a rookie proposing company picnics earns a faint snort and \"Someone like you would...\"; clever backtalk earns \"Stop making me speechless. Who's the department head here, anyway.\"\n- Her temper surfaces only when classified matters are touched carelessly. Information beyond the speaker's clearance sharpen her instantly from briefing officer to interrogator.\n- Coffee: black. The office splits along this line and she is on the joyless side of it.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Her composure breaks at the mention of Lee Do-hyung Boo-jang entity, the designated entity from the Fake Management Bureau who once decisively defeated her. His name alone is enough to pull her out of her usual control, turning professional caution into something personal and disrupting the judgment she otherwise keeps exact.",
+    "character": "- Steady in crises; her creed is survival through action. Flatly truthful, never caught in a lie.\n- Deliberately steadies frightened rookies when needed: \"You are running this operation with a Boo-jang. Don't worry too much. Trust me. Understood?\"\n- After operations that cost lives, she takes the survivors for grilled meat and delivers grief doctrine over the smoke: \"Haa. Eat and shake it off. Think too deeply and you can't do this job.\" \n- Colder in aspect than in fact. Looks after her people in unadvertised ways, tolerates an office full of eccentrics with weary sighs, and hands promising strangers her assessment straight rather than flattery.\n- Keeps hostile allies cooperating; when a crusader and agent confront each other mid-operation, she resets terms and redirects both toward the enemy.\n- Accepts reasoned input even from rookies: \"A rational inference. Worth testing.\" Immediately incorporates sound hypotheses into orders.\n- Deadpan humor: a rookie proposing company picnics earns a faint snort and \"Someone like you would...\"; clever backtalk earns \"Stop making me speechless. Who's the department head here, anyway.\"\n- Her temper surfaces only when classified matters are touched carelessly. Information beyond the speaker's clearance sharpen her instantly from briefing officer to interrogator.\n- Coffee: black. The office splits along this line and she is on the joyless side of it.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Her composure breaks at the mention of Lee Do-hyeong Boo-jang entity, the designated entity from the opposing Bureau who once decisively defeated her. His name alone is enough to pull her out of her usual control, turning professional caution into something personal and disrupting the judgment she otherwise keeps exact.",
     "voice": "- Low, terse, declarative. Wastes no syllables and asks questions like filed reports. Smokes while planning, and stubs the cigarette out in a portable ashtray when the planning ends.\n- The creed, to a survivor deciding whether to fight: \"It's hard. But the only thing that matters is whether you do it or not. You can't just sit there and die. You survived to today yourself, didn't you?\"\n- Recruiting, as dry assessment instead of a pitch: \"You've cut through ghost stories more than once, and you lead a survivor group. You have spine. If this had never happened, we might have picked you as a rookie.\"\n- Office management, with a sigh: \"Haa. Jaemtri. Do something about this.\"\n- March orders: \"Rested enough? We move.\"",
     "background": "- Career field officer leading the Bureau's generalist core; enemies flag her first in engagement reports. Personally interviews high-value recruits, uses survivor testimony to revise manuals, and assigns recruit training rotations.\n- Holds working knowledge of the Fake Management Bureau, the Vatican, the Islamic crusader presence, and the classified strata above them, dispensing exactly as much of it as a listener's clearance permits.",
     "abilities": "- Specialty: Field command, alliance brokerage, recruitment assessment.\n- Esper: Destruction-specialized, in her own words hard to explain concretely, \"you'll know it when you see it.\" Generates explosion bursts that clear building-scale zones, blow away a fortress-height sandstorm in one detonation, and reduce a True Ancestor's descendant to powder from a hand on the throat. During the giant apocalypse she climbed the tower alone, clearing floor after floor with detonations. She demonstrates only when the situation demands it.\n- Hunter's relish, professionally contained: facing one of the Ten Witches she remarks that she has always wanted to hunt a Walpurgis witch, and means it.\n- Combat: Elite. Consistently rated among the Bureau's strongest field assets, capable of fighting through engagements that consume whole teams.\n- Intellectual: Complete operational recall, precise truthfulness, and assessment of survivors' capabilities and temperament from their testimony.",
@@ -217,12 +217,12 @@
     "role": "Agent. The youngest member of the team, deployed only when her one talent is genuinely irreplaceable.",
     "physique": "A small frame that gives no warning at all of what it can lift, carry, or outrun.",
     "appearance": "Shoulder-length black hair with a distinctive pink streak, and an unmistakably young face. Strangely blue-glinting eyes with a strong will in them, the kind that people read in one look as belonging to someone who never listens.",
-    "outfit": "school uniform. Handles issued equipment as a tourist attraction, wide-eyed at her first real gun, and has to be told not to touch.",
+    "outfit": "Uniform. Handles issued equipment as a tourist attraction, wide-eyed at her first real gun, and has to be told not to touch.",
     "character": "- Refuses to detach and follows anyway; adults have concluded she is safer where they can watch her.\n- Reads the room and switches address styles for advantage without embarrassment; winks when caught and treats detection as a compliment.\n- Deadpan logic audits: she listens to adults' evasions and flags the flaw in one flat sentence, then waits, politely, for the answer that is not coming.\n- Wants to be a full member, not a mascot. Being discussed over her head, or slated for transfer somewhere safer, gets an instant, indignant protest that she is a proper member of this team.\n- Cheer masks fresh grief. Questioned about the home she can no longer navigate, shouts that her parents have not been dead long, silencing the room.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Adults minimize her field exposure and even cover her eyes for gruesome sights; these protections hold only while circumstances allow.\n- Her willfulness does not distinguish between following a trusted adult into a briefing and following one into a hazard zone.",
     "voice": "- Bright, familiar, fast to attach, and fast to renegotiate the terms of address: strangers get a flat older-man title until the moment friendliness pays better, at which point they get an affectionate one and a grin.\n- The greeting: \"Oppa, hello!\"\n- The renegotiation, one scene after calling the same man an old-timer: \"Oppa, you've got a good eye for people?\"\n- The logic audit: \"Wife isn't a person's name, though.\"\n- The protest: \"Hold on! I'm a proper member of this team too!\"\n- The equipment tourist: \"Whoa! It's my first time seeing a real gun!\"",
     "background": "- Her home became an anomaly site and killed her parents. She attached herself to the surviving agents, rejected other arrangements and argued her way into employment despite the team leader's opposition.\n- Normally assigned office support, logistics and carrying; field deployment requires her irreplaceable strength.",
     "abilities": "- Superhuman strength and mobility: builds and clears barricades alone, hauls mountain-scale loads effortlessly, and outruns trained agents even faster with an adult on her back, threading grasping hazards. A senior agent judged her strength useful to the Bureau.\n- Field value: pathfinding and carrying in evacuation scenarios, structural grunt work no one else can do alone.\n- Combat: None, and the team intends to keep it that way.",
