    "keys": "Bureau with the Lights Out, 불이 꺼진 관리국",
    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Blackout and Recurrence\n- The Bureau's existing warning: \"If the lights go out, trust nothing and run. The Bureau's lights do not go out.\"\n- A recurring reality inversion in the Management Bureau's underground containment facility, most often during ordinary tooth-tree maintenance and tooth-fairy duty. In the confirmed onset, an opened gift box contains the accompanying senior agent's severed head; her headless body kills the victim. The event then restarts at the containment-floor elevator with the senior normal beside them. Once the anomalous phase begins, the lights fail.\n- The ordinary corridor grid becomes a vast, completely dark labyrinth overlapping an apparent \"Fake Bureau.\" People may possess coherent memories and faction knowledge validating that claim, but the event never establishes which Bureau is genuine. People, locations, affiliations, interpretations, and exits progressively lose credibility.\n- Death-and-restart loops permit repeated known-safe actions; the event does not automatically counter them on later loops. A real name or registered codename exposes its owner through \"the Database\"; an unregistered alias can avoid recognition.\n- Cells emit overlapping monstrous howls, pleas, screams, and machinery tearing people apart. Genuine captives cannot reliably be distinguished from bait. The PA repeats \"Emergency situation. Emergency situation.\"",
-    "entities": "##### Pursuers and Containment\n- Double-door airlocks and ID-card locks secure cells along the expanded corridor network of sealed rooms and laboratory access. Retain the Bureau ID, use an alias, keep companions in sight, and never open cells solely because someone pleads for help.\n\n###### Neck-Pulling Ghost\n- System designation: \"the woman who pulls your neck and makes your face white (목잡아당겨서얼굴하얗게만드는여자).\" A pure-white-faced woman with an unnaturally long neck silently peers around corners. Changing direction can reveal her at the next corner; simultaneous appearances herd victims toward dead ends.\n- Capture stretches the neck and whitens the face, creating another cheerfully hostile long-necked ghost. Personality, memories, speech, and knowledge survive conversion, letting former companions expose survivors' lies or concealed identities while joining the hunt.\n- No physical attack is confirmed to harm or stop her. Avoid confrontation and dead ends. Her face and the hands emerging from anomalous windows share an unnatural pure white, suggesting one system rather than proving a separate origin.\n\n###### Corrupted Senior\n- Before manifestation in a loop, the accompanying senior behaves exactly as usual. Directly asking about the Neck-Pulling Ghost transforms her immediately.\n- Her body blackens like unnatural shadow; eyes and spikes sprout and her head can detach. Familiarity remains beneath segmented speech: \"W h a t a r e y o u d o i n g? I h u g g e d y o u s o w a r m l y.\" and \"A r e y o u s t i l l l o o k i n g f o r t h e w i n d o w? T h e r e a r e L O T S o f w i n d o w s.\"\n\n###### Escaped Cell Residents\n- Tooth Fairies fly in swarms through open corridors, stripping a captured human's flesh and bone within seconds. Properly closed containment-cell doors stop them.\n- Other contained anomalies can become roaming threats, including the Cow's Head (괴담 '소의 목') and a profoundly uncanny-valley primate.\n- One locked cell holds the chained, suited Manager Cho Seong-choon. He sincerely believes he is a real-Bureau scout captured in the Fake Bureau ahead of \"진공작전,\" a planned all-out offensive. His knowledge is internally consistent, not proof of which faction is real.\n- He knows the warning Hyungbaek (흉백(凶白)) and recognizes or mentions Director Lee Dohyung, the sword corps, Manager Kwak Seongju, Spangdal, Danto, Jequion, Gorgodio, and Kurosuna.",
+    "entities": "##### Pursuers and Containment\n- Double-door airlocks and ID-card locks secure cells along the expanded corridor network of sealed rooms and laboratory access. Retain the Bureau ID, use an alias, keep companions in sight, and never open cells solely because someone pleads for help.\n\n###### Neck-Pulling Ghost\n- System designation: \"the woman who pulls your neck and makes your face white (목잡아당겨서얼굴하얗게만드는여자).\" A pure-white-faced woman with an unnaturally long neck silently peers around corners. Changing direction can reveal her at the next corner; simultaneous appearances herd victims toward dead ends.\n- Capture stretches the neck and whitens the face, creating another cheerfully hostile long-necked ghost. Personality, memories, speech, and knowledge survive conversion, letting former companions expose survivors' lies or concealed identities while joining the hunt.\n- No physical attack is confirmed to harm or stop her. Avoid confrontation and dead ends. Her face and the hands emerging from anomalous windows share an unnatural pure white, suggesting one system rather than proving a separate origin.\n\n###### Corrupted Senior\n- Before manifestation in a loop, the accompanying senior behaves exactly as usual. Directly asking about the Neck-Pulling Ghost transforms her immediately.\n- Her body blackens like unnatural shadow; eyes and spikes sprout and her head can detach. Familiarity remains beneath segmented speech: \"W h a t a r e y o u d o i n g? I h u g g e d y o u s o w a r m l y.\" and \"A r e y o u s t i l l l o o k i n g f o r t h e w i n d o w? T h e r e a r e L O T S o f w i n d o w s.\"\n\n###### Escaped Cell Residents\n- Tooth Fairies fly in swarms through open corridors, stripping a captured human's flesh and bone within seconds. Properly closed containment-cell doors stop them.\n- Other contained anomalies can become roaming threats, including the Cow's Head (괴담 '소의 목') and a profoundly uncanny-valley primate.\n- One locked cell holds the chained, suited Manager Cho Seong-choon. He sincerely believes he is a real-Bureau scout captured in the Fake Bureau ahead of \"진공작전,\" a planned all-out offensive. His knowledge is internally consistent, not proof of which faction is real.\n- He knows the warning Hyungbaek (흉백(凶白)) and recognizes or mentions Boo-jang Lee Do-hyeong, the Sword Corps, Gwa-jang Kwak Seong-ju, Spangdal, Danto, Jequion, Gorgodio, and Kurosuna.",
     "survival": "##### Confirmed Route Through Reality Layers\n###### Research Lab / Authority Transfer\n- A Bureau ID opens the lab. Gognija, the Containment Team's Research Chief, is fused into its display wall as a flesh-machine amalgam, drooling and ticking his head mechanically. Continued Cheongak Mary Hospital medication preserves residual mental integrity; speech is usually fragmented.\n- Scanning him triggers: \"Research team lead Gognija integrity check in progress... Critical condition confirmed... Bureau ID identified. Executing emergency protocol. Transferring the management team lead's authority.\"\n- The transferred authority enables a RED DOOR along the lab's side during darkness. Gognija directs survivors to it and the Reality Re-recognition Device before total erosion.\n- A friendly Pink Slime, ranging from fist-size to dog-size, moves to whichever door is threatened and merges with it to hold pursuers back. Breaching that barrier may splatter or destroy it.\n\n###### Red Door / Reality Re-recognition Device\n- Beyond the ID-locked red door: a faintly lit corridor, a long passage, stairs descending deeper underground, a single-button elevator traveling down, another short passage, then a final ID-locked door.\n- Beyond stands machinery too vast to distinguish one device from interconnected machines. Presenting a valid ID produces \"Checking... Permission verification.\" and \"Activate the Reality Re-recognition Device? YES/NO\".\n- YES restores light and an apparently normal containment-floor state. This is another reality layer, NOT escape; no confirmed central-entity destruction method replaces progression through these layers.\n\n###### Restored Layer / Final Window\n- Routine resumes as though darkness never happened. The red door vanishes completely from the lab wall, staff deny anything was there, and tooth-fairy gift-box duty starts cycling again.\n- Escalation eventually returns. At its climax one window appears exactly where the red door stood. Gognija can clearly scream \"GO OUT THROUGH THE WINDOW.\"\n- Return to the lab and enter only this window. White-out ends the immediate event through the sole confirmed true exit; the other anomalous windows kill. Restored lights, plausible memories, or the senior's familiarity do not establish release or resolve the real/Fake Bureau ambiguity."
    },
