    "keys": "해피엔딩, 해피엔딩 홀",
    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Identity and Forced Recruitment\n- A holy site of Mumyeong Chanran-gyo's Happy Ending Sect (해피엔딩 교단); each sect has its own Hall. This mobile location anomaly attaches to the next real-world ritual site and leaks paranormal phenomena while anchored. Capacity varies by sect from one occupant to tens of thousands. The rumor that it is a larger creature's stomach is unconfirmed.\n- A member establishes a recruitment hook with invitations such as \"Come with me\" or \"Let's go together.\" Answering confirms it, making transfer difficult or impossible to stop. Break sight and block the voice before completion; enclosed-space distortion signals active transfer onset.\n- The interior resembles an old reinforced-concrete fallout shelter: rusted exposed walls, sparse lights, cement finish, connected domes and arched corridors, no ordinary windows. An ant-warren layout separates lay housing, rituals, brewing, and the Power Zone.",
-    "space": "##### Initiation Route and Layout\n- Initiation begins by murdering someone the applicant sincerely wishes happiness for, often a relative, and bringing the body. In the central Great Rotunda / Coffin Hall, a huge vaulted chamber of empty and occupied coffins, the applicant eulogizes the deceased as a good person and prays for happiness. An elderly officiant raises both hands to chant \"Be happy. Be happy. Be happy…\" and the congregation repeats it during daily mourning and initiation. Corpses go to the black disposal box at one end or directly toward brewing.\n- East / West — Initiate Living Quarters: cramped bunk cells without privacy. About one hundred ordinary-clothed lay initiates are unified by Tongue Parasites rather than uniforms. Mandatory shared breakfast and dinner in the eastern Cafeteria transmit the parasite through conversation, replace tongues, and integrate recruits into shared cognition. Avoid communal meals and conversation with them.\n- South — Hidden Brewing Facility: behind a coffin leaning against the wall, a flimsy white rectangular vat roughly two people tall holds around one hundred bodies; surrounding pipes emit alcoholic vapor. Final initiation, \"graduation,\" has converted initiates assemble outside, march single-file over the upper pipework, and voluntarily dive into the alcohol, drowning as the active ingredient of substitute Sinseonju. The cult believes drinking it lets one \"hear Lord Name and see the Happy Ending.\"\n- Power Zone (권능 구역): isolated, larger domes with higher ceilings and no CCTV house officers and anomaly-bearing \"infected guests\"; a \"lion's enclosure.\"\n- North — Concealed Exit Corridor: at the Power Zone's empty far end, a small fixed glass viewport near the ceiling looks up into Jisan Village for officers to inspect the surface. This is the only identified surface-associated route; no guaranteed extraction procedure is established.",
+    "space": "##### Initiation Route and Layout\n- Initiation begins by murdering someone the applicant sincerely wishes happiness for, often a relative, and bringing the body. In the central Great Rotunda / Coffin Hall, a huge vaulted chamber of empty and occupied coffins, the applicant eulogizes the deceased as a good person and prays for happiness. An elderly officiant raises both hands to chant \"Be happy. Be happy. Be happy…\" and the congregation repeats it during daily mourning and initiation. Corpses go to the black disposal box at one end or directly toward brewing.\n- East / West — Initiate Living Quarters: cramped bunk cells without privacy. About one hundred ordinary-clothed lay initiates are unified by Tongue Parasites rather than uniforms. Mandatory shared breakfast and dinner in the eastern Cafeteria transmit the parasite through conversation, replace tongues, and integrate recruits into shared cognition. Avoid communal meals and conversation with them.\n- South — Hidden Brewing Facility: behind a coffin leaning against the wall, a flimsy white rectangular vat roughly two people tall holds around one hundred bodies; surrounding pipes emit alcoholic vapor. Final initiation, \"graduation,\" has converted initiates assemble outside, march single-file over the upper pipework, and voluntarily dive into the alcohol, drowning as the active ingredient of substitute Sinseonju. The cult believes drinking it lets one \"hear Ireum-nim and see the Happy Ending.\"\n- Power Zone (권능 구역): isolated, larger domes with higher ceilings and no CCTV house officers and anomaly-bearing \"infected guests\"; a \"lion's enclosure.\"\n- North — Concealed Exit Corridor: at the Power Zone's empty far end, a small fixed glass viewport near the ceiling looks up into Jisan Village for officers to inspect the surface. This is the only identified surface-associated route; no guaranteed extraction procedure is established.",
     "entities": "##### Lee Seo-yu and Her Powers\n- A cheerful adolescent officer with the 5th Class Power \"Death Stager,\" wearing an old, worn school uniform and red headband. She introduces herself by full real name and twin status. The performative \"cute schoolgirl officer\" persona hides fear of Lord Name and of being forgettable.\n- Originally recruited by the Capacity-Praising Sect, she rejected its slow-pain doctrine and self-mutilation Powers, defecting by swallowing a Happy Ending scripture. She has consumed seven anomalies; mastery varies.\n- Death Stager (사망연출자), her secondary mastered ability: her head detaches alive along a clean horizontal cut, rolls away leaving a long red trail, then expands into a giant mouth-and-tongue cavity to swallow a target. Within, red-pulsing flesh, circulatory walls, and vein-like ropes draw the victim deeper. The head whispers \"Let's go together\"; any verbal response triggers irreversible full ingestion. Silence is the only safe answer.\n- Body-Segmenting Power: the only one of her seven consumed anomalies fully mastered, producing clean transversal severances of bodies.\n\n##### Seeker in the Box (상자 속 구도자)\n- A 6th Class Power of the Capacity-Praising Sect. A devotee severs their own legs and seals themselves in a black box; years of meditation, agony, and digestive secretion fuse body and box into a soft-bodied digesting creature. Its lid displays the remaining victim quota (정원).\n- Inert at a distance, it opens when a suitable target is in range and extends two pale hands along the ground, palms up. Approaching counts as acceptance even when involuntary, including being pushed. Do not approach. Once tracking begins, the box reappears closer each minute, eventually directly ahead whenever the target turns their head; remain absolutely still until another countermeasure becomes available.\n- Swallowed victims occupy soft membrane pouches filled with digestive fluid that preserves consciousness while dissolving them over an average of 27 years. The Seeker narrates each victim's suffering into every occupant's mind, exposing them to each other's broadcasts. It stays closed until all occupants are completely digested, then undergoes a long recovery while feeding on bulk flesh.",
     "notes": "##### Scriptures and Tongue Parasites\n- Sacred Law Scriptures (신성법 경전): glowing parchment fragments with one verse, though some appear blank. Swallowing one makes the eater an anomaly's embodiment and grants its Power, which demands expression through their own weirdness, cruelty, fear, or strangeness. Acolytes commonly swallow several, with differing mastery.\n- Tongue Parasite: a horror folk-derivative of Cymothoa exigua. It anchors at the tongue base, consumes and replaces the tongue while preserving normal speech, and leaves a worm-like tip with its own jaws. Speech during shared meals suffices for transmission; the resulting shared cognitive substrate makes hosts think and agree alike and repeat ritual phrases naturally."
    },
