   "세광역": {
-   "keys": "Segwang Station, Forest of the Dying, 세광역, 임종의 숲",
+   "keys": "Segwang Station, Forest of the Dying, 세광역, 임종의 숲, 임종의 숲길",
    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Mandatory Arrival and Founding\n- A station sub-anomaly within sealed Segwang Special City. Every successful entry, regardless of route or method, ends here: entrants materialize unconscious, sprawled on the Platform, then awaken without experiencing the transfer. They never initially awaken in the Concourse, another station, or the surface.\n- The plaque bears the paid-advertisement-style subtitle \"Forest of the Dying Path.\" Its identity merged with the real-world suicide hotspot \"■■■ Forest,\" crossed by the line.\n- Nearest major stop to City Hall, the wider disaster's origin, it received roughly seven thousand evacuees and became the line's largest stronghold. Failed communications, exhausted food, continuing surface catastrophe, and absent rescue drove them to collective suicide. The station varied around their choice; the Forest is that population, not a separate predator that killed it.\n- Some hanging bodies bear pen-written palm testaments. One reads:\n\n  No one is coming to save us  \n  Seven thousand were abandoned  \n  We want to run  \n  but there is no way out  \n  so we become trees instead\n\n- The Forest recruits later entrants into the same conclusion through despair, suggestion, separation, and surrender. City Hall's proximity also makes the station important for reaching the unresolved disaster's center.",
     "space": "##### Platform and Forest Concourse\n- The subway shelters entrants from the surface's extinction-class disaster, which does not normally project directly underground; the station's own anomaly remains active.\n- The Platform has ordinary subway architecture and dim but usable light. It is the main staging, rest, regrouping, and fallback area while the Forest stays upstairs. The opposite-track side remains collapsed and unreachable while the Forest is active; a staircase at the usable Platform's end ascends to the Concourse.\n- Above are earth, dead leaves, trees, and dense humid fog. Thick trunks alternate with hanging human bodies whose clothing carries years of dust; corpses are too numerous to count. A blindly reached-for branch may be a human foot. Sound is unnaturally dead apart from transit audio and recruitment voices.\n- The etiquette board stands near the entrance stairs; the cash transit-card machine and turnstiles lie deeper inside, requiring passage through the Forest. Protective charms and similar wards rapidly mold and physically collapse while carried.\n\n##### Station Office and Institute Access\n- A reinforced-glass door separates the ordinary concourse Station Office from public space. Desks, cabinets, lost property, and transit administrative materials remain; a Segwang Transit Corporation Employee ID can be obtained from personnel, remains, or stored property.\n- Terminating the Forest makes the opposite-direction platform accessible. There, a staff-only machine/communications-room steel door accepts that ID and opens into the Institute Core Layer beneath Segwang Station. An ID alone does not make the platform reachable. Ordinary train departure follows the registration procedure above and does not require terminating the Forest.",
